{
 "about": "ZoomFrames, 2026-10-17, seed 1, AMD Radeon Pro 5500M (4 GB VRAM), the harness's headless Chrome at 1280x800, each build served from its own dir and port, the default load (warm of one sim day, speed 600), ?bench=zoom,orbit,turn,pan on one load, one 12 s run per bench after the warm. base: fa2974a plus the peers' uncommitted sim edits in the tree at 03:31 (src/sim only). new: the tree at 04:40 with this change (and the peers' sim edits since). Not a quiet machine: peers' runs between and maybe during the runs. Frames over 20 ms are counted (16.7 ms counts vsync jitter, Page1s): page dt from the bench's six slowest gaps, worker GPU from its twelve slowest frames.",
 "changes": {
  "smallsSlices": "src/gpu/tiers/lumped.ts steps(t): a lumped kind's step given in slices, the split dispatched SPLIT_BINS (2^14) bins at a time (wgsl/lumped.ts lumpSplit over bins lo to hi), yielding after each; step(t) runs them all. src/gpu/smalls.ts slices(t): the day as those slices (day(t) runs them all); its law returns them. src/gpu/store.ts: a Law's run may return an iterable of slices; beginSteps flushes after each and beginPaced paces them (pace: submit, then wait for the GPU to finish what went before the last pace, so one slice runs while the next is queued and the frames go between). src/gpu/animals.ts: the spin-up paces each slice of the smalls' days before anyone wakes.",
  "firstLevelLists": "webgpu.js frontAsk(views, ahead): the levels and bearings the page says it shows next are built first; frontsReady() lists the island levels and bearings whose front lists are all built, posted with frameDone when it changes (worker.js). live.js prefetch(views) (was a no-op) and listsReady(view). play/main.js: a zoom's goal (camera.goalView) is prefetched (live.goal, unused, removed); each bench waits until its first view's lists are built (the zoom's first frame is the whole island at zoom 0), at most LISTS_MS 20 s, and records listsWaitMs.",
  "isleGpu": "webgpu.js drawView: a far or front list with nothing in it is not walked (five empty far sources and the empty static front list each cost about 0.6 ms at the island levels, a workgroup a cell); an empty front list is done as soon as its count is read. setSources: a source builds front lists whenever its keep pass's storage buffers fit the device's limit, so the logs (reader and driver ring, ten of ten) walk front lists instead of their far list."
 },
 "identity": "Store hash of seed 1 (src/gpu/store.ts hash, random brain, a worktree at fa2974a, scratch script): after the first tick 68aece9e4ab7ffb7 and after the first midnight's landing (t 86461) c66f2aff2d719599, equal before and after the change (the spin-up's ten smalls days and the midnight law both run sliced).",
 "smallsDay": "bun, seed 1, GPU timestamps per dispatch, after the first tick: the smalls' day is 2.8 to 3.0 s of GPU time, of it the three lumped splits (tiller 0.26 to 0.35 s, litter 1.1 to 1.2 s, fauna 1.3 s; per-bin compute, the same on a second day); the eaten kernel 2 to 16 ms. Sliced at 2^16 bins the slices took at most 84 ms, at 2^15 44 ms; the sum stays 2.8 to 2.9 s.",
